When Cursor auto-generates a Git commit message for this repository (Source Control sparkle / Generate Commit Message), you MUST use Conventional Commits.

Do NOT copy this repo’s older git history. Old messages look like “Add Auto Carry to Mount Daun.” That style is deprecated.

Required format (single subject line, no trailing period, lowercase description, imperative, max 72 chars):

<type>(<optional-scope>): <short why>

Types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, style, chore, perf, revert
Scopes when useful: loader, sempat-ui, rayfield, windui, tabs, or a game slug (mount-daun, capybara-onsen)

Output ONLY the commit message. No quotes, no markdown, no preamble.

Good:
feat(mount-daun): add auto carry and auto accept carry
fix(mount-noxera): wait for GameplayPaused before summit teleports
docs: add agent knowledge base and commit rules

Bad:
Add Auto Carry to Mount Daun.
update stuff
WIP
Fixed bug
